<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1593) <span class="when">Oct 14, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Any window starts tabs.</b> Click <b>+</b> at the right of a floating window&#8217;s title bar and pick another open window: the two become tabs of one window. Have as many groups as you like.</li>
<li><b>Drag to combine, reorder and take out.</b> Drag a window by its title bar onto another&#8217;s tabs or title bar to join it; drag a tab sideways to reorder it, or down off the strip to make it a window again.</li>
<li><b>Scroll arrows.</b> When a group&#8217;s tabs don&#8217;t fit, &#8249; and &#8250; at the ends step through them. A group is never narrower than its widest window needs.</li>
<li><b>Tabs with news.</b> A Pull Plates or Queue tab behind another shows a dot when a pull ends: green finished, amber frames to check, red a plate failed.</li>
<li><b>Notes in a window.</b> The arrow in the notes list&#8217;s header puts the notes in a window of their own, which can be a tab; close it and they are back beside the picture.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1476) <span class="when">Oct 12, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>DPX sequences play.</b> 8, 10, 12 and 16-bit DPX files open and play like any other image sequence, read as the color space set for DPX in Settings, Color.</li>
<li>A tall floating Playlist with thumbnails could stop the app. Fixed.</li>
<li>Small fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1441) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Network is in the Review menu.</b> Review ▸ Network; it was under Window. It is also in the right-click Review menu.</li>
<li><b>A playlist on a network drive no longer slows the window.</b> Whether each clip's file is there is checked in the background.</li>
<li><b>Locate Media… reads a folder in the background.</b> A line above the toolbar says how far it has got.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1430) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Small fixes.</li>
</ul>
